  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on a single live trial in a small Swedish village, which may limit their applicability to larger urban areas or different cultural contexts.",
      "what": "This study conducted a scenario-based multi-actor-multi-criteria analysis (MAMCA) during a live autonomous delivery robot (ADR) trial in the village of Veber%d, Sweden. It evaluated the preferences of multiple stakeholder groups simultaneously, finding that participants favored ADR systems capable of managing high shipment volumes and diverse goods while supporting the local economy, social ties, and environmental goals.",
      "why": "It shifts the evaluation of autonomous delivery systems from isolated stakeholder perspectives to a collective, socio-technical framework, demonstrating that community acceptance in small settlements depends on local social and economic values rather than purely commercial or operational metrics."
